est":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121836","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121836","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121836.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121836.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Brief Description\r\nSome enum items of `Monitor` are left without use when compiling a template with specific options (see `Testing` section). This PR addresses these cases.\r\n\r\n~Also fixes `modules/csg/csg_shape.cpp` not compiling with `disable_physics_3d=yes`.~ Fixed by #122593 & #121168\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\nCompiled using the following options: `target=template_release dev_mode=yes optimaze=speed d3d12=no accesskit=no` with each of:\r\n- `disable_navigation_2d=yes` ✅\r\n- `disable_navigation_3d=yes` ✅\r\n- `disable_physics_2d=yes` ✅\r\n- `disable_physics_3d=yes` ✅\r\n- With all of the above combined ✅\r\n- `disable_3d=yes` ✅\r\n- With all of the above combined ✅\r\n\r\n## Additional Info\r\nI've tested these changes more after rebasing against master (to 00932449c9f372b30301d8b5fdc1be70ec12b5c0 commit [in these changes](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/compare/17f53fcaa66f43d3316612925272e88fec2cc19b..25e6345036696dd8337fcd45d135b7db2b4334f5)), and found an error in my assumptions, which was corrected in latest force-pushed commit ([link to changes](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/compare/25e6345036696dd8337fcd45d135b7db2b4334f5..f2e9920c4cbdfe5d913b35585c05128be7753a14)). Would really appreciate if anyone have the time to test these changes, you can do so by trying to compile these changes with `scons` using the options in `Testing` section.\r\n\r\n## Use of AI\r\nNo AI was used in the process of making these changes.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121836/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.